# The finish of a fold of one limb (milestone2.md, "When something is not finite"): the final
# state when it is finite, with the flag true; otherwise the canonical NaN and the flag false.
# Which infinity an IEEE sum of the operands would have given is not computed: D5's "not finite,
# which value is unspecified", made a definite value.
kernel:        fold_finish_1
input:         s
output:        r
output:        mask flag
value:         s
ensures:       finite_or_nan r flag=flag
min_precision: 1
source:        the finish of a fold: the state or the canonical NaN (milestone2.md)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeFoldFinish.v fold_finish_1_correct
cone_exempt:   the output is a select after an explicit test that s is finite (flag), which is what the kernel claims

a    = abs(s)
flag = lt(a, const inf)
r    = select(flag, s, const nan)
